  "query_preview": "..\n(Tomorrow through Friday)\nIssued at 1125 AM CDT Fri Oct 16 2026\n\nA low impact forecast will exist for much of the extended\nforecast. Saturday is shaping up to be absolutely fantastic for\nthose who favor light winds, seasonably cool temperatures, low\nhumidity and plenty of sun. Despite continued low afternoon\nhumidities, the lighter winds will lead to improved fire weather\nconditions for southeast Oklahoma, and an additional Fire Danger\nStatement appears unnecessary. Additional frost development should\noccur Saturday night into Sunday morning across northern parts of\nthe forecast area, with overnight lows being close to those \nexpected tonight. Another Frost Advisory may be warranted. \n\nSoutherly winds make a return to the area on Sunday, which will\nlead to warmer afternoon temperatures. Upper level ridging builds\ninto the Central United States by early next week and persists\nthrough much of the upcoming week. This will keep warmer\ntemperatures across the region, with near to above normal highs\nreturning as early as Monday and certainly by Tuesday. The next\nchance of rain looks to accompany another strong storm system that\nmakes its way eastward toward the area late in the week and into\nthe next weekend. Low rain chances will return ahead of this\nfeature possibly as early as Thursday-Friday, but with a trend\ntoward a more delayed arrival, more likely over the next weekend.",
